# Conclave product rules

Read **CONCLAVE.md** at the repo root for the full handbook. Keep it accurate when product rules change.

## Levels (only three)

- **Member** — Identity only (photo, name, role, ambitions, looking for). Verification fields are optional.
- **Verified** — Identity + all 3 credentials: business email, LinkedIn, resume
- **BLACK** — paid ($50/mo or $500/yr) or earned; never granted by peer invite

Short version: Identity → Member. Skip verification → stay Member. Add email + LinkedIn + resume → Verified.

Do not block signup on verification. Optional extras (website, registration, portfolio) do not replace the three.

## BLACK CONNECTION ≠ BLACK

Peer invites award BLACK CONNECTION only. They never promote someone to BLACK.

## Plans vs levels

Premier ($20/mo) is a plan that expands who Members can meet. Standing levels are Member / Verified / BLACK.

## UX

- Level badges: matching metal marks — steel / champagne / black (BLACK is the coolest)
- BLACK CONNECTION: black checkmark badge (not a chain icon)
- Never show “Tier N · Name”
- Signup: Identity required; verification optional (skip = stay Member)
- Discover cards: even height, no “verified via LinkedIn/email” list
- Plans: one grouped Free / Premier / BLACK block
- Signup highlights missing Identity sections when incomplete
- Top nav fixed on every screen

## Demo

`brianasome@gmail.com` / `Brian812` is the fixed demo owner login. Demo env flags stay off in production unless intentionally enabled.

## Delivery

Website first in the browser. Native app later after the website makes money. No phone-frame shell for web.
